  "headline": "DPR RI Officially Passes Asset Recovery Law After 18-Year Delay",
  "seoTitle": "DPR RI Passes Asset Recovery Law",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian House of Representatives has passed the Asset Recovery Law, allowing for the seizure of assets from illegal investment schemes.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Indonesian House of Representatives officially enacted the Asset Recovery Law following an 18-year legislative standstill.",
    "The regulation allows for the seizure of assets from perpetrators of fraudulent investment schemes to compensate victims.",
    "The Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK) stated it is prepared to implement the new law following a thorough internal review."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives (DPR RI) has formally passed the Asset Recovery Law, concluding a legislative process that spanned 18 years. The newly enacted legislation is intended to serve as a key mechanism in the national effort to combat corruption. Members of the House Commission III have specified that the law provides authority to seize assets acquired through illegal investment activities, facilitating the return of funds to victims of such fraud. Following the law's passage, the Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK) announced its intention to comply with the new regulatory framework. While the law has garnered support, it has also faced scrutiny regarding its provisions on illicit enrichment. The enactment is widely characterized by some observers as a notable development during the leadership of President Prabowo Subianto in the context of anti-corruption initiatives.",
